From dd0d2c612d0771281c2dc4656af68922176bb02d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 28 Jun 2026 17:09:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 04717/11362] [outer-loop] In-context verified-pattern lever:
 honest AMBIGUOUS/underpowered + source-code OBFUSCATION-blocked (corrects
 over-claimed null)

Operator's clarified idea: give the small LLM a top-K of verified worked+failed PATTERNS as IN-CONTEXT
reasoning exemplars (not weight pre-training) from source code + 60 solves + human solves. Genuinely-
untried (verified vs the nulled weight-transfer exp4318/4342, single-recipe router exp4556, efficiency-
retrieval exp4933). Built: arc_pattern_library (library + retriever + LOO + SOURCE-CODE extractor) +
7 tests + arc_incontext_pattern_proposal_ab (LOO opening-shift A/B).

Adversarial sub-agent review (GAPS_FOUND) corrected an over-claimed 'null' -> the honest read is:
- AMBIGUOUS + UNDERPOWERED: execution-relevant LEADING delta ~0 (CI incl 0, n<=8). The earlier
  single-sample +0.33 'flicker' was LLM stochasticity (M=3 denoising washed it out). The positional
  metric is BIASED against exemplars (rewards degenerate constant-run digit overlap) -> not the headline.
- SOURCE-CODE OBFUSCATION-BLOCKED (the decisive finding for the operator's specific input): ARC-AGI-3
  game source is fully obfuscated (random identifiers; verified 13/25 source patterns semantically empty,
  e.g. 'def win(self): self.nkuphphdgrp = True'). So 'break apart the source code into patterns' extracts
  STRUCTURE but not SEMANTICS -> ~0 transferable signal. The behavior-derived patterns (solve traces +
  registry win-conditions, which ARE semantic) showed no opening shift.
- Rediscovers arc_solve_learning.py:114: few-shotting a weak 9B below a confidence bar can degrade.

NOT closed: a properly-powered test (M>=5, all 25 games) + a de-obfuscation-aware extractor would settle
the behavior-pattern half; the source-code half is blocked by obfuscation. Ledger updated so it is not
re-tried as 'untried'. adversarial_verify clean.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
